Sure! To compare the declaration flags of your two objects, just pass their stringified (JSON) representations to the `areDeclarationFlagsIdentical` function. For example:

```ts
const left = JSON.stringify(parameterObject);
const right = JSON.stringify(variableDeclarationObject);

const result = areDeclarationFlagsIdentical({ left, right });
console.log(result); // true if flags match, false otherwise
```

Could you share the stringified versions of `parameterObject` and `variableDeclarationObject` so I can run the comparison for you?
